      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Five underground coal mines operated in Van Lear from 1910 until 1946, fueling the town’s economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_Lear%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Van Lear Historical Society’s Coal Miner’s Museum houses mining equipment, photos, and personal items that tell the town’s coal‑camp story.",
